[size=4][b][u]Palette Configuration Reference[/u][/b][/size]

This is the complete reference for players who want to create custom colors, text styles, transparency, outlines, and faction artwork. The [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/MarketingSites/NexusMods/ComponentLibrary.bbcode]component library[/url] shows which HUD sections and components use these values.

The detailed palette rules are maintained in the repository's palette schema and reference documentation.
The Scaleform/ActionScript resolver adds required-role, allowlist, reference,
and compatibility checks. A palette must satisfy both.

Use the [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/MarketingSites/NexusMods/UserConfiguration.bbcode]player configuration guide[/url] for simple theme
switching and the [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/MarketingSites/NexusMods/LayoutConfigurationReference.bbcode]layout configuration reference[/url]
for all other XML elements.

[size=3][b][u]Included palettes and public themes[/u][/b][/size]

Each of the four themed release variants packages all five palette XML files under [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI\palettes[/font]. The themed variant controls only the initial [font=Courier New]palette[/font] attribute in [font=Courier New]layout.xml[/font]. Minimalist packages no palette files; its build resolves the [font=Courier New]starfield.xml[/font] color roles to literals before staging its external layout and six component fragments.

[list][*]Public appearance — Palette filename[/*][/list]
[list][*]Venworks Customizable HUD - Venworks Theme — [font=Courier New]venworks.xml[/font][/*][/list]
[list][*]Venworks Customizable HUD - Trackers Alliance Theme — [font=Courier New]trackers-alliance.xml[/font][/*][/list]
[list][*]Venworks Customizable HUD - Freestar Collective Theme — [font=Courier New]freestar-collective.xml[/font][/*][/list]
[list][*]Venworks Customizable HUD - Crimson Fleet Theme — [font=Courier New]crimson-fleet.xml[/font][/*][/list]
[list][*]Included neutral Starfield option — [font=Courier New]starfield.xml[/font][/*][/list]

All five packaged palettes currently resolve their [font=Courier New]faction.logo[/font] roles to SVG
files included with the HUD.

[size=3][b][u]Runtime path and selection[/u][/b][/size]

Palette files load only from:

[code]
Data\Interface\VenworksCUI\palettes\
[/code]

The root layout selects one palette by filename:

[code]
<venworksCUI schemaVersion="1" runtimeVersion="1"
             designWidth="1920" designHeight="1080"
             safeLeft="64" safeTop="36"
             safeRight="64" safeBottom="36"
             palette="venworks.xml">
[/code]

The filename must:

[list]
[*]begin with an ASCII letter or number;[/*]
[*]contain only letters, numbers, dots, underscores, and hyphens before [font=Courier New].xml[/font];[/*]
[*]contain no more than 60 characters before the extension under the current pattern;[/*]
[/list]
[list]
[*]name one file directly in [font=Courier New]VenworksCUI\palettes[/font]; and[/*]
[*]contain no [font=Courier New]..[/font], slash, backslash, colon, query string, or fragment.[/*]
[/list]

The loaded palette is limited to 65,536 characters. There is no live palette
switching. Fully exit and restart Starfield after changing the selection or
palette content.

If the root layout omits [font=Courier New]palette[/font], literal-only version 1 layouts remain
supported. Any [font=Courier New]@palette.*[/font] reference without a selected palette is invalid.

[size=3][b][u]Document structure[/u][/b][/size]

A [font=Courier New]venworksCUIPalette[/font] document has exactly five sections in this exact order:

[code]
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<venworksCUIPalette schemaVersion="1">
  <colors>
    <color role="foreground.primary" value="#F4FBFF" />
  </colors>
  <typography>
    <style role="body" font="$MAIN_Font" fontSize="16"
           bold="false" color="foreground.primary" />
  </typography>
  <opacities>
    <opacity role="opaque" value="1" />
  </opacities>
  <strokes>
    <stroke role="panel" color="panel.border"
            opacity="muted" width="2" />
  </strokes>
  <assets>
    <asset role="faction.logo" kind="svg"
           value="venworks-logo.svg" />
  </assets>
</venworksCUIPalette>
[/code]

The root requires only [font=Courier New]schemaVersion="1"[/font]. Unknown root or section attributes,
extra sections, missing sections, reordered sections, child content inside an
entry, and unknown entry attributes are rejected.

The abbreviated sample above illustrates structure but is not a valid runtime
palette because it omits required roles. Start custom work from a complete
packaged palette or the complete template later in this document.

[size=3][b][u]Semantic role names[/u][/b][/size]

Every entry has a unique [font=Courier New]role[/font] within its own category. Roles:

[list]
[*]use lowercase ASCII letters and numbers;[/*]
[*]begin each dot-separated segment with a lowercase letter;[/*]
[*]may contain hyphens inside a segment;[/*]
[*]use dots to express semantic hierarchy; and[/*]
[*]contain at most 64 characters.[/*]
[/list]

The effective pattern is:

[code]
[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\.[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)*
[/code]

The same role text may exist in different categories because colors,
typography, opacities, strokes, and assets have separate namespaces.

Additional non-required roles are allowed within the category limits and may be
referenced by compatible layout attributes.

[size=3][b][u]Section counts[/u][/b][/size]

[list][*]Section — Entry element — Minimum — Maximum[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]colors[/font] — [font=Courier New]color[/font] — 1 — 64[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]typography[/font] — [font=Courier New]style[/font] — 1 — 16[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]opacities[/font] — [font=Courier New]opacity[/font] — 1 — 32[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]strokes[/font] — [font=Courier New]stroke[/font] — 1 — 32[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]assets[/font] — [font=Courier New]asset[/font] — 1 — 32[/*][/list]

[size=3][b][u]Colors[/u][/b][/size]

A color entry requires exactly [font=Courier New]role[/font] and [font=Courier New]value[/font]:

[code]
<color role="accent.primary" value="#19C8FF" />
[/code]

[font=Courier New]value[/font] must be six-digit [font=Courier New]#RRGGBB[/font]. Three-digit shorthand, eight-digit alpha,
CSS names, functions, and unprefixed hex values are rejected. The runtime
normalizes accepted colors to uppercase when resolving them.

[size=2][b][u]Required color roles[/u][/b][/size]

[list][*]Role — Intended semantic use[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]foreground.primary[/font] — Primary readable text and foreground artwork.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]foreground.muted[/font] — Secondary labels and de-emphasized foregrounds.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]accent.primary[/font] — Main theme accent and focus color.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]accent.secondary[/font] — Supporting accent.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]panel.background[/font] — Panel and recess backgrounds.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]panel.border[/font] — Panel outlines and dividers.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.normal[/font] — Normal interactive/composite foreground state.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.selected[/font] — Selected or active state.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.disabled[/font] — Disabled or unavailable state.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.clear[/font] — Clear/safe status.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.caution[/font] — Caution status.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.danger[/font] — Danger status.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]state.critical[/font] — Critical/hostile status.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]meter.health[/font] — Player health meter.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]meter.oxygen[/font] — Oxygen meter.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]meter.carbondioxide[/font] — CO2 meter.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]meter.boost[/font] — Boost meter.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]marker.player[/font] — Player marker.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]marker.ally[/font] — Ally/friendly marker.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]marker.hostile[/font] — Hostile marker.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]marker.objective[/font] — Objective marker.[/*][/list]

All 21 roles are required even if a particular custom layout does not visibly
consume every role.

[size=3][b][u]Typography[/u][/b][/size]

A typography entry requires exactly [font=Courier New]role[/font], [font=Courier New]font[/font], [font=Courier New]fontSize[/font], [font=Courier New]bold[/font], and
[font=Courier New]color[/font]:

[code]
<style role="heading" font="$MAIN_Font_Bold" fontSize="22"
       bold="true" color="foreground.primary" />
[/code]

[list][*]Attribute — Contract[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]font[/font] — Exactly [font=Courier New]$MAIN_Font[/font] or [font=Courier New]$MAIN_Font_Bold[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]fontSize[/font] — Integer 1 through 128.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]bold[/font] — Exactly [font=Courier New]true[/font] or [font=Courier New]false[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]color[/font] — Name of an existing color role in the same palette, without [font=Courier New]@palette.colors.[/font].[/*][/list]

Required typography roles are [font=Courier New]body[/font], [font=Courier New]label[/font], and [font=Courier New]heading[/font].

Typography references expose resolved fields individually:

[code]
@palette.typography.heading.font
@palette.typography.heading.fontSize
@palette.typography.heading.bold
@palette.typography.heading.color
[/code]

Each field may be used only on the identically named attribute of a [font=Courier New]<text>[/font]
element. A typography role cannot be applied to a component as a single style
object.

[size=3][b][u]Opacities[/u][/b][/size]

An opacity entry requires exactly [font=Courier New]role[/font] and [font=Courier New]value[/font]:

[code]
<opacity role="panel" value="0.94" />
[/code]

The value must be a plain decimal from [font=Courier New]0[/font] through [font=Courier New]1[/font]. Scientific notation,
negative values, and values over 1 are rejected.

Required opacity roles are:

[list][*]Role — Intended semantic use[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]opaque[/font] — Fully visible generated content.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]panel[/font] — Standard panel opacity.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]muted[/font] — De-emphasized fills, strokes, or empty meters.[/*][/list]

An opacity reference may resolve only an attribute named [font=Courier New]opacity[/font] or ending in
[font=Courier New]Opacity[/font].

[size=3][b][u]Strokes[/u][/b][/size]

A stroke entry requires exactly [font=Courier New]role[/font], [font=Courier New]color[/font], [font=Courier New]opacity[/font], and [font=Courier New]width[/font]:

[code]
<stroke role="panel" color="panel.border"
        opacity="muted" width="2" />
[/code]

[list][*]Attribute — Contract[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]color[/font] — Existing color role in the same palette.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]opacity[/font] — Existing opacity role in the same palette.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]width[/font] — Integer 0 through 64.[/*][/list]

The required stroke role is [font=Courier New]panel[/font].

Stroke fields resolve separately:

[code]
@palette.strokes.panel.color
@palette.strokes.panel.opacity
@palette.strokes.panel.width
[/code]

[list]
[*][font=Courier New]color[/font] is compatible with [font=Courier New]strokeColor[/font] and [font=Courier New]divider@color[/font].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]opacity[/font] is compatible with [font=Courier New]strokeOpacity[/font].[/*]
[*][font=Courier New]width[/font] is compatible with [font=Courier New]strokeWidth[/font].[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][u]Assets[/u][/b][/size]

An asset entry requires exactly [font=Courier New]role[/font], [font=Courier New]kind[/font], and [font=Courier New]value[/font]:

[code]
<asset role="faction.logo" kind="svg" value="venworks-logo.svg" />
[/code]

The required asset role is [font=Courier New]faction.logo[/font].

[size=2][b][u]SVG asset kind[/u][/b][/size]

[font=Courier New]kind="svg"[/font] requires one packaged filename matching this shape:

[code]
[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,59}.svg
[/code]

Palette SVG assets must be single files directly under
[font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI\Assets[/font]; subdirectories and [font=Courier New]..[/font] are rejected.

The production faction-display fragment consumes [font=Courier New]faction.logo[/font] through
[font=Courier New]<svg src="@palette.assets.faction.logo">[/font]. Therefore a palette used with the
production layout must declare [font=Courier New]faction.logo[/font] as [font=Courier New]kind="svg"[/font], even though the
general palette schema permits the other asset kinds.

[size=2][b][u]Built-in icon asset kind[/u][/b][/size]

[font=Courier New]kind="icon"[/font] requires one of these allowlisted same-domain icons:

[code]
health          oxygen        co2             shield
armor           weapon        aiming          ship
vehicle         fuel          cargo           scanner
stealth         warning       objective       jolly-roger
death           poison        burning         electrocution
disease
[/code]

An icon asset reference is compatible only with [font=Courier New]icon@name[/font].

[size=2][b][u]Embedded symbol asset kind[/u][/b][/size]

[font=Courier New]kind="symbol"[/font] requires one allowlisted Bethesda HUD symbol:

[code]
environment-alert
quest-door-marker
boost-fill
vehicle-exit-prompt
[/code]

A symbol asset reference is compatible only with [font=Courier New]symbol@name[/font]. Symbol
availability remains specific to the owning normal or large HUD movie.

[size=3][b][u]Reference syntax and compatibility[/u][/b][/size]

References must occupy the complete layout attribute value. They are not string
interpolation.

[list][*]Category — Syntax — Compatible destination[/*][/list]
[list][*]Color — [font=Courier New]@palette.colors.<role>[/font] — [font=Courier New]color[/font] or an attribute ending in [font=Courier New]Color[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*]Opacity — [font=Courier New]@palette.opacities.<role>[/font] — [font=Courier New]opacity[/font] or an attribute ending in [font=Courier New]Opacity[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*]Typography — [font=Courier New]@palette.typography.<role>.<field>[/font] — Identically named [font=Courier New]font[/font], [font=Courier New]fontSize[/font], [font=Courier New]bold[/font], or [font=Courier New]color[/font] on [font=Courier New]<text>[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*]Stroke — [font=Courier New]@palette.strokes.<role>.<field>[/font] — [font=Courier New]strokeColor[/font]/[font=Courier New]divider@color[/font], [font=Courier New]strokeOpacity[/font], or [font=Courier New]strokeWidth[/font] according to field.[/*][/list]
[list][*]Asset — [font=Courier New]@palette.assets.<role>[/font] — [font=Courier New]svg@src[/font], [font=Courier New]icon@name[/font], or [font=Courier New]symbol@name[/font] matching the asset kind.[/*][/list]

Examples:

[code]
color="@palette.colors.foreground.primary"
fillOpacity="@palette.opacities.panel"
font="@palette.typography.heading.font"
fontSize="@palette.typography.heading.fontSize"
bold="@palette.typography.heading.bold"
strokeWidth="@palette.strokes.panel.width"
src="@palette.assets.faction.logo"
[/code]

Invalid examples include:

[code]
value="Color: @palette.colors.accent.primary"
width="@palette.colors.accent.primary"
visible="@palette.opacities.opaque"
src="@palette.assets.some-icon"
[/code]

The last form is invalid when [font=Courier New]some-icon[/font] is declared as [font=Courier New]kind="icon"[/font], because
an icon asset can resolve only [font=Courier New]icon@name[/font], not [font=Courier New]svg@src[/font].

[size=3][b][u]Complete custom-palette starter[/u][/b][/size]

This template contains every required role. Save a customized copy under a new
safe filename instead of overwriting a packaged palette.

[code]
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<venworksCUIPalette schemaVersion="1">
  <colors>
    <color role="foreground.primary" value="#F4FBFF" />
    <color role="foreground.muted" value="#8EB9D0" />
    <color role="accent.primary" value="#19C8FF" />
    <color role="accent.secondary" value="#6BE7FF" />
    <color role="panel.background" value="#061722" />
    <color role="panel.border" value="#2DCBFF" />
    <color role="state.normal" value="#F4FBFF" />
    <color role="state.selected" value="#19C8FF" />
    <color role="state.disabled" value="#536D7A" />
    <color role="state.clear" value="#64E572" />
    <color role="state.caution" value="#FFD800" />
    <color role="state.danger" value="#FF7B21" />
    <color role="state.critical" value="#FF3C54" />
    <color role="meter.health" value="#D34A5B" />
    <color role="meter.oxygen" value="#35E6E6" />
    <color role="meter.carbondioxide" value="#FFB51B" />
    <color role="meter.boost" value="#6D8CFF" />
    <color role="marker.player" value="#F4FBFF" />
    <color role="marker.ally" value="#64E572" />
    <color role="marker.hostile" value="#FF3C54" />
    <color role="marker.objective" value="#19C8FF" />
  </colors>
  <typography>
    <style role="body" font="$MAIN_Font" fontSize="16"
           bold="false" color="foreground.primary" />
    <style role="label" font="$MAIN_Font" fontSize="14"
           bold="false" color="foreground.muted" />
    <style role="heading" font="$MAIN_Font_Bold" fontSize="22"
           bold="true" color="foreground.primary" />
  </typography>
  <opacities>
    <opacity role="opaque" value="1" />
    <opacity role="panel" value="0.94" />
    <opacity role="muted" value="0.7" />
  </opacities>
  <strokes>
    <stroke role="panel" color="panel.border"
            opacity="muted" width="2" />
  </strokes>
  <assets>
    <asset role="faction.logo" kind="svg"
           value="venworks-logo.svg" />
  </assets>
</venworksCUIPalette>
[/code]

[size=3][b][u]Custom-palette workflow[/u][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Fully exit Starfield.[/*]
[*]Copy one complete palette, preferably the closest visual starting point.[/*]
[*]Rename the copy with a safe unique filename such as [font=Courier New]my-hud.xml[/font].[/*]
[*]Keep all required roles and the five required sections in their original order.[/*]
[*]Change semantic values rather than renaming roles consumed by the production layout.[/*]
[*]If changing [font=Courier New]faction.logo[/font], place a supported SVG directly under [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI\Assets[/font] and use its filename only.[/*]
[*]Set [font=Courier New]layout.xml[/font] to [font=Courier New]palette="my-hud.xml"[/font].[/*]
[*]Restart Starfield and test normal, aiming, scanner, combat, low-health, vehicle, large-HUD, and target-aspect-ratio states.[/*]
[*]Keep the custom palette and any custom SVG in a personal override mod so a release update does not overwrite them.[/*]
[/list]

When changing status colors, preserve clear differentiation among clear,
caution, danger, and critical states. When changing typography, test the longest
localized strings and both normal and large HUD movies.

[size=3][b][u]Failure behavior[/u][/b][/size]

Palette failures use categorized diagnostics:

[list][*]Diagnostic — Typical cause[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI PALETTE MISSING[/font] — Selected filename is not deployed under [font=Courier New]palettes[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI PALETTE MALFORMED[/font] — XML is not well formed.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI PALETTE UNSUPPORTED[/font] — [font=Courier New]schemaVersion[/font] is not [font=Courier New]1[/font].[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI PALETTE INVALID[/font] — Missing/duplicate role, wrong section order, bad value, unknown reference, or incompatible reference destination.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI PALETTE SECURITY ERROR[/font] — Unsafe filename/path or unsafe SVG asset value.[/*][/list]
[list][*][font=Courier New]CUI ASSET LOAD ERROR[/font] — A resolved SVG is absent, unreadable, or outside the supported SVG subset.[/*][/list]

Because loading is atomic, a palette error prevents the full configurable HUD
layer from displaying. Correct the first diagnostic, restart Starfield, and
verify the result in game.
